{{also|hitüp}}
==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|hits up|hitting up|hit up|hit up}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|informal}} To contact with a [[request]] or [[demand]]; to [[touch base]].
#: ''Why not '''hit him up''' for some assistance on the rebuilding project?''
# {{lb|en|transitive|informal}} To [[talk]] with (someone) about a [[desire#Verb|desired]] [[subject]]; to [[chat up]] (esp. a friend).
#: ''I'd like to '''hit him up''' about last episode, but he's working all night.''
# {{lb|en|intransitive|informal}} To take an intoxicating drug.

